{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"ALSA-2026:19137","published":"2026-05-19T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-05-26T16:59:30.243794759Z","related":["CVE-2026-32283","CVE-2026-33816"],"summary":"Important: go-fdo-server security update","details":"This package provides a server-side implementation of the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) specification, written in Go. FDO is an open standard for the late binding of device credentials, allowing for automated and secure on-boarding of devices when they are first powered on in their final location.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * github.com/jackc/pgx/v5: github.com/jackc/pgx: Memory-safety vulnerability (CVE-2026-33816)\n  * crypto/tls: golang: Go crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple TLS 1.3 key update messages (CVE-2026-32283)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/go-fdo-server"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.1-1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:19137.json"}},{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server-manufacturer","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/go-fdo-server-manufacturer"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.1-1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:19137.json"}},{"package":{"name":"go-fdo-server-owner","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/go-fdo-server-owner"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.0.1-1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:19137.json"}},{"pac